@ifnottex
@node Top
@top multi-region: select several pieces of text at once

Emacs normally lets you select one piece of text at a time.
multi-region lets you select several.  In ``I love ClaudeAI very much''
you can have @emph{love} and @emph{much} selected@comma{} and nothing else@comma{} then copy
both with one key.

It works in text@comma{} Org@comma{} Markdown and code buffers@comma{} in read-only buffers
such as eww@comma{} in EPUB books (nov.el)@comma{} and in PDFs (pdf-tools or
pdf-canvas).  In a PDF you can select passages on several pages and copy
them in one go.

Open this manual with @code{C-h R multi-region} or @code{C-c M h}.  In it@comma{} @code{i}
looks up a command or option by name and @code{s} searches the text.

@end ifnottex

