@node Turning it on
@section Turning it on

@findex multi-region-mode
@findex global-multi-region-mode

Put the folder of multi-region on your load path and add this to your
init file:

@lisp
(require 'multi-region)
(global-multi-region-mode 1)
@end lisp

To try it in one buffer only@comma{} use @code{M-x multi-region-mode} instead.

The mode line shows @samp{MR} while the mode is on@comma{} and @samp{MR[3]} when three
pieces are selected.

@node A first try
@section A first try

@enumerate
@item
Open any text.  Hold @code{Control} and drag the mouse over a word.  It
stays highlighted.
@item
@code{C-drag} over another word@comma{} further on.  Both are highlighted.
@item
Press @code{M-w}.  Both words are copied@comma{} one per line@comma{} and deselected.
@item
Changed your mind?  @code{C-c M /} selects them again.
@end enumerate

That is most of it.  The rest of this manual is details.

@node Selecting
@chapter Selecting

@menu
