* With the keyboard::
@end menu

@node With the mouse
@section With the mouse

@findex multi-region-mouse-drag

@multitable {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Mouse
@tab What it does
@item @code{C-drag}
@tab Add the dragged text to the selections
@item @code{C-double-click}
@tab Add the word under the pointer
@item @code{C-triple-click}
@tab Add the line under the pointer
@item @code{C-click}
@tab Deselect the selection under the pointer@comma{} or select a picture
@end multitable

You can start the usual way: drag@comma{} or @code{C-SPC} and move.  As soon as
you @code{C-drag} somewhere else@comma{} that first region becomes a selection too.
So ``drag@comma{} then C-drag@comma{} then C-drag'' works as in a word processor.

Selections that touch or overlap become one.

@node With the keyboard
@section With the keyboard

@findex multi-region-toggle
@vindex multi-region-thing

@code{C-c M SPC} does what makes sense at point:

@itemize
@item
with an active region@comma{} it selects the region;
@item
inside a selection@comma{} it deselects it;
@item
otherwise@comma{} it selects the picture or the word at point.
@end itemize

The ``word'' can be something else: see @samp{multi-region-thing} in @ref{Options, , Options}.

@node Using the selections
@chapter Using the selections

All commands are under the prefix @code{C-c M}.  This manual uses that
key; if you prefer another@comma{} see @ref{Other keys, , Other keys}.

@multitable {aaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Key
@tab What it does
@item @code{C-c M w}
@tab Copy all selections as one piece of text (also @code{M-w})
@item @code{C-c M k}
@tab Kill all selections (also @code{C-w})
@item @code{C-c M r}
@tab Replace every selection with the same text
@item @code{C-c M x}
@tab Run a region command on every selection
@item @code{C-c M n}
@tab Jump to the next selection
@item @code{C-c M p}
@tab Jump to the previous selection
@item @code{C-c M u}
@tab Deselect the most recent selection
@item @code{C-c M c}
@tab Deselect everything
@item @code{C-c M /}
@tab Bring back what was last deselected all at once
@item @code{C-c M h}
@tab Open this manual
@end multitable

