@node Copying and killing
@section Copying and killing

@findex multi-region-copy
@findex multi-region-kill
@findex multi-region-kill-ring-save
@findex multi-region-kill-region
@vindex multi-region-separator
@vindex multi-region-keep-after-copy

@code{M-w} and @code{C-w} act on the selections while there are any@comma{} and behave
as usual when there are none.  You don't have to think about it.

Copied pieces are joined with a newline.  For a different separator just
this once@comma{} use @code{C-u C-c M w} and type it.  To change it for good@comma{} set
@samp{multi-region-separator}.

Copying deselects everything@comma{} so you can start fresh.  Set
@samp{multi-region-keep-after-copy} to keep the selections instead.

A word that a PDF split with a @samp{¬} is joined again: ``inflam¬ mation''
is copied as ``inflammation''.

@node Changing all selections at once
@section Changing all selections at once

@findex multi-region-replace
@findex multi-region-do

@code{C-c M r} asks for a text and puts it in place of every selection.

@code{C-c M x} asks for a command and runs it on each selection as if it were
the region.  Good ones to try: @samp{upcase-region}@comma{} @samp{comment-region}@comma{}
@samp{fill-region}.

@code{C-/} (undo) puts the text back after either@comma{} and after @code{C-w}.

@node Moving between selections
@section Moving between selections

@findex multi-region-next
@findex multi-region-previous

@code{C-c M n} and @code{C-c M p} move point to the next and previous selection.

@node Deselecting and bringing back
@section Deselecting and bringing back

@findex multi-region-remove-last
@findex multi-region-clear
@findex multi-region-restore
@findex multi-region-keyboard-quit

@code{C-c M u} deselects the selection you made last.  @code{C-c M c} deselects
everything.

@code{C-c M /} brings back what was last deselected all at once@comma{} whether by
@code{C-c M c}@comma{} by copying@comma{} or by @code{C-g} in a PDF or EPUB@.  Selections you
made since are kept.

It works after changing the text too:

@itemize
@item
after @code{C-c M r}@comma{} it selects the replacements@comma{} so you can carry on
with them;
@item
after @code{C-w}@comma{} undo first (@code{C-/}) to put the text back@comma{} then @code{C-c M /}
selects it again.
@end itemize

@node Pictures
@chapter Pictures

@vindex multi-region-image-margin

A picture in the buffer is selected whole or not at all.  Drag across it
with the text around it@comma{} or @code{C-click} it to select it alone.  A selected
picture gets a band in the selection color; @samp{multi-region-image-margin}
sets its width@comma{} and 0 turns it off.

This works for pictures in eww and EPUBs@comma{} and for inline images in Org
(@code{C-c C-x C-v}) and Markdown (@code{C-c C-x C-i}).  In Org and Markdown@comma{} a link
to a picture file counts even when the picture isn't shown.

Copying takes only the text.  The pictures are for packages that build
notes from your selections@comma{} such as readq; see @ref{For other packages, , For other packages}.

